Approaches learned from (no files copied)
-----------------------------------------

Botbench's design learned from these projects. No file, function or text of theirs is stored in this repository;
where an approach was followed, it was written again for Botbench, and the decision records in docs/adr/ say which.

- OpenMausBot (Apache License 2.0): driving each coding tool as a child process over its own headless protocol
  (docs/adr/0001-own-codebase-driving-vendor-clis.md, docs/reviews/design-vs-openmausbot.md). Nothing from its
  enterprise/ folder.
- Paperclip (MIT License): watching a repository's labelled issues, retrying GitHub's limits, and the review of the
  peers design (docs/adr/0008-watch-issues.md, docs/adr/0004-peers-direct-messages.md).
- Rakazo (Apache License 2.0): approaches for workbenches that work together (docs/adr/0004-peers-direct-messages.md).

